[Example Rules]
Rule 10 (valid 2D transposed convolution)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : int, v_4 : int} |= ndim(v_1) = 4 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 4 ∧ v_3 ≥ 1 ∧ v_4 ≥ 0 ∧ v_3 × (shape(v_1, 2) − 1) + shape(v_2, 2) − 2 × v_4 > 0 ∧ v_3 × (shape(v_1, 3) − 1) + shape(v_2, 3) − 2 × v_4 > 0

Rule 1 (tensor shapes should be the same)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) − 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)

Rule 3 (input tensors must have the same number of dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2)

Rule 23 (3-dimensional tensor with all positive shape dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 3 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) − 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0

Rule 24 (tuple of ints represents valid shape dimensions)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_1.len - 1] : v_1[i] > 0

